Firstly, I added up all the given numbers:
```
10 + 20 + 30 + 40 + 50 = 150
```

Next, I divided this sum by the number of values, which is 5 in this case:
```
150 / 5 = 30
```

So, the average of these numbers is **30**.

To confirm this, you can check if the sum of the deviations from the mean (average) equals zero. In this case, it does:

```
(10-30) + (20-30) + (30-30) + (40-30) + (50-30) = -60 + -60 + 0 + 10 + 20 = 0
```

Therefore, the average of the numbers 10, 20, 30, 40, and 50 is indeed **30**.
